# Wireframe: App Shell (Mobile)

## Purpose & Flow Context

Mobile layout for authenticated pages at viewport <768px. The sidebar is hidden behind a hamburger menu and opens as an overlay with backdrop. Entry: user authenticates on mobile or resizes to <768px. Exit: user resizes to >768px, logs out, or navigates within the content area. This wireframe covers the mobile-hidden state and the mobile-overlay state. Theme variants (Light/Dark/System) are not separate wireframes — theme changes only visual tokens (CSS custom properties owned by the design-system), not layout structure. This mobile wireframe applies identically to all theme states; the ThemeToggle component and DS color tokens handle visual variation.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

Same as desktop shell. Mobile-specific behaviors noted.

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: Single-column layout (12-col collapses to full-width single column). Spacing cadence: 8px.

**App-shell**: Header with hamburger + full-width content. Sidebar appears as overlay.

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Header | Sticky bar: hamburger button (visible), search trigger, notification bell, user avatar, theme toggle | Full width |
| Content | Main page content — full viewport width | overflow-y: auto |
| Sidebar overlay | Slides in from left above content, with backdrop | z-index: 300; 280px width |

**Content hierarchy** (by visual priority):
1. Header — hamburger for navigation access, global triggers
2. Content — primary task takes full width
3. Sidebar overlay — on-demand navigation

---

### State: Mobile-Hidden (Default)

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  Header: [☰] [search] [theme-toggle] [bell 3] [avatar]          |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|  (Page content takes full viewport width)                         |
|                                                                    |
|  [h1 Page Title]                                                  |
|                                                                    |
|  Content area scrolls independently.                              |
|  Sidebar is hidden off-screen.                                    |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### State: Mobile-Overlay (Sidebar Open)

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  Header: [✕] [search] [theme-toggle] [bell 3] [avatar]          |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  +-- Overlay (280px) --+                                         |
|  |  [Team Name    ▼]   |  (Content dimmed behind backdrop)       |
|  |                     |                                         |
|  |  [icon] Issues  ●   |                                         |
|  |  [icon] Projects    |                                         |
|  |  [icon] Cycles      |                                         |
|  +---------------------+                                         |
|  |← Backdrop (full remaining area, semi-transparent, clickable)→||
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

*Legend: [{Button}] [Input] [Link] [#Heading] [>Dropdown] [Avatar] [Icon]; ☰ = hamburger; ✕ = close overlay*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Hamburger button | HamburgerButton | Visible at <768px; aria-label="Open menu" when closed, "Close menu" when open | Toggles sidebar overlay visibility |
| Sidebar overlay | Sidebar (mobile-overlay) | Slides from left edge; 280px width; z-index above content | Focus trapped inside when open |
| Backdrop | Backdrop | Semi-transparent overlay; click or Escape to close | aria-hidden="true" when closed |
| Header elements | Header | Same triggers as desktop; full width | Hamburger replaces collapsed sidebar |
| Nav links | NavLink | Same as desktop; full labels visible in overlay | aria-current="page" on active |
| Team selector | TeamSelector | Same behavior; full dropdown within overlay | — |
| Theme toggle | ThemeToggle | In header, consistent across desktop/tablet/mobile; not duplicated in overlay | Persisted to localStorage |

## Data Display

No data display on the overlay — it is a navigation panel. Content area is a pass-through container for page-specific content.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| Hamburger | "Open menu" / "Close menu" | Dynamic label based on overlay state |
| Backdrop | (decorative — no label) | role="presentation"; aria-hidden="true" |
| Nav links | "Issues", "Projects", "Cycles" | Same labels as desktop |
| Close button in overlay | "Close menu" | Applies when hamburger shows X icon |

## States

### Populated — Mobile-Hidden (Default)

Layout as shown above. Sidebar hidden; hamburger visible in header. Content takes full width.

### Populated — Mobile-Overlay

Layout as shown above. Sidebar slides in from left at 280px. Backdrop covers remaining viewport. Header hamburger icon changes to X.

### Empty

N/A — layout shell always renders. Page content states are per-page.

### Loading

Skeleton in content area; header and hamburger render immediately.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  Header: [☰] [search] [theme-toggle] [bell] [avatar]            |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|  [===== skeleton bar =====]                                       |
|  [=== skeleton ===]                                               |
|  [======== skeleton =========]                                    |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Error

No layout-specific error state. Page errors display in content area.

### Success / Confirmation

N/A for layout shell. Overlay close/closing is immediate visual feedback.

### Sidebar Overlay Open/Close Transition

| Action | Mechanism |
|--------|-----------|
| Open (tap hamburger) | Sidebar slides in from left over 250-300ms ease-out; backdrop fades in simultaneously |
| Close (tap backdrop) | Sidebar slides out to left; backdrop fades out |
| Close (tap nav link) | Navigate + sidebar closes simultaneously |
| Close (Escape key) | Sidebar closes; focus returns to hamburger |
| Close (resize >768px) | Overlay closes; sidebar returns to side-by-side layout |

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Mobile (<768px) | Full-width content; sidebar overlay with hamburger; touch targets ≥44px recommended |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Side-by-side layout; sidebar returns; overlay/hamburger hidden |
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full desktop layout |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | header role="banner", nav role="navigation" on overlay sidebar, main role="main" on content |
| Heading order | h1 from page content; no layout heading |
| Reading / Focus order | Header (hamburger first) → Content. When overlay opens: focus moves to first nav link in sidebar |
| Accessible names | Hamburger: aria-label="Open menu" / "Close menu". All icon-only controls have aria-label |
| Keyboard operability | Tab: header triggers → content (when closed). Overlay open: focus trapped; Tab cycles links; Escape to close |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation (≥44px recommended on mobile for touch) |
| Focus not obscured | Overlay is on top when open; backdrop prevents interaction with content |
| Non-color intent | Active link uses background + icon fill; close icon indicates overlay dismiss |
| Focus management | Overlay opens → focus to first nav link. Overlay closes → focus returns to hamburger |

*Defer to design-system: pixel contrast, focus-appearance, per-component target-size/keyboard.*
